// Generated by scripts/tessaya/docs-bundle.mjs from docs/user; edit those pages, then run it.
export const DOCS_FEATURES_MD =
  '# Everything Tessaya does\n\nOne short page per feature: what it is for, what to say, and where it lives. Tessaya\'s **Help** reads this page, so\nthe same words show in her window, in the browser and in her own answers. The longer guides are linked from each one.\n\n## Use Help\n\nPress **Ctrl+K** in Tessaya\'s window and type what you want to do. Pages, settings and these features come up as you\ntype; pick one with Enter. Type a question instead ("how do I insert my address?") and choose **Ask Tessaya**: she\nanswers from this page and says which feature it came from. If nothing here covers it, she says so rather than\nguessing. **F1** opens Help beside the page you are on, already showing what that page is for. In a browser, Help is\nunder Settings → Tessaya → Help. You can always just ask her out loud: "how do I make a snippet?"\n\n**Lessons** in Help walk you through a few steps each. A step ticks itself once you have used the\npage it teaches, on any device: a step done from your phone shows as done on your computer.\n\nEach feature says **Live** (on your devices now), **Beta** (works, still changing) or **Coming** (planned, not here\nyet).\n\n## First run\n\n<!-- id: first-run | task: set Tessaya up the first time | status: live | area: start | place: help | on: desktop | for: new | guide: getting-started.md -->\n\nSet Tessaya up in about a minute: your microphone, your dictation key, one sentence, and who does the work.\n\nTry saying: "run setup again"\n\n1. The first time you open Tessaya\'s window the setup starts by itself.\n2. To run it again later, open **Help** and choose **Run setup again**.\n\n## Learn Tessaya and tips\n\n<!-- id: learn | task: learn what Tessaya can do | status: live | area: start | place: learn | on: desktop, web, phone | for: new -->\n\nOne short tip a day on the page it is about, and a list of every tip with what you have already tried.\n\nTry saying: "what can you do?" · "teach me something new"\n\n1. Open **Learn Tessaya** at the bottom of the sidebar.\n2. Lessons are at the top; tips you have tried have a tick.\n\nGood to know: Tips can be daily, all at once or off. Turning them off on one device turns them off everywhere.\n\n## Install and update\n\n<!-- id: install | task: install or update Tessaya | status: live | area: start | place: about | on: desktop, web | for: new | guide: install.md -->\n\nInstall the desktop app, and keep it and your server up to date.\n\nTry saying: "check for updates" · "what\'s new in you?"\n\n1. Settings → About shows the version you are on and checks for updates.\n2. Ask her what is new and she tells you what changed in plain words.\n\n## Themes and the look\n\n<!-- id: themes | task: change the look | status: live | area: start | place: appearance | on: desktop, web, phone | for: new | guide: appearance.md -->\n\nPick a palette (Woad, Damson or Madder), light or dark, and how much things move.\n\nTry saying: "use the Damson theme" · "switch to dark mode"\n\n1. Settings → Appearance.\n2. The T3 window follows the palette you pick here, unless you chose a theme there yourself.\n\n## Keyboard and mouse\n\n<!-- id: keys | task: change a shortcut | status: live | area: start | place: keys | on: desktop | for: maker | guide: keybindings.md -->\n\nChange the dictation key, the screen shortcut and what your mouse buttons do.\n\nTry saying: "change the dictation key"\n\n1. Settings → Keyboard and mouse.\n2. Click a shortcut, then press the keys you want.\n\nGood to know: Mouse buttons can be bound on Windows only.\n\n## Dictation\n\n<!-- id: dictation | task: type by speaking | status: live | area: talk | place: dictation | on: desktop, web, voice | for: new | guide: tessaya-dictation.md#start -->\n\nSpeak and your words are typed into whatever app you are in.\n\nTry saying: "start dictating" · "stop dictating"\n\n1. Click in any text box.\n2. Hold **Alt+Win**, speak, and let go. Your words are typed where the cursor is.\n3. Press **Esc** before you let go to throw it away.\n\nGood to know: Recognition runs on this computer by default, and nothing you say leaves it.\n\n## Spoken punctuation and lists\n\n<!-- id: punctuation | task: dictate lists and punctuation | status: live | area: talk | place: dictation | on: desktop, voice | for: new | guide: voice-input.md -->\n\nSay the punctuation and layout you want while you dictate.\n\nTry saying: "new line" · "bullet point" · "full stop"\n\n1. Dictate as usual and say "new line", "comma" or "bullet point" where you want them.\n\n## Dictation clean-up\n\n<!-- id: cleanup | task: have my dictation tidied | status: live | area: talk | place: dictation | on: desktop, web, phone, voice | for: new | guide: tessaya-dictation.md#good-to-know -->\n\nHave your words tidied as they are typed: misheard words, grammar and false starts.\n\nTry saying: "turn clean-up off" · "set my spelling to American"\n\n1. Dictation → **Clean up with AI**: Claude, On this computer, or Off.\n2. Spelling is British by default; American or "as heard" are there too.\n\nGood to know: Clean-up is one setting on every device you use.\n\n## Names and words she gets wrong\n\n<!-- id: names | task: get names and words right | status: live | area: talk | place: dictation | on: desktop, voice | for: maker | guide: voice-input.md -->\n\nTeach her the names and terms you use, so dictation spells them right.\n\nTry saying: "learn the word Zayd"\n\n1. Correct a word after dictating and she learns it.\n2. Dictation → **Words** lists what she learned, newest first, each with ✕ to undo.\n\n## Languages\n\n<!-- id: languages | task: dictate in more than one language | status: live | area: talk | place: dictation | on: desktop, voice | for: maker | guide: tessaya-dictation.md -->\n\nDictate in more than one language and say which ones you speak.\n\nTry saying: "only English and Urdu"\n\n1. Dictation → Languages, or tell her which languages you speak.\n\n## Writing style per app\n\n<!-- id: style | task: make dictation sound like me | status: live | area: talk | place: style | on: desktop, voice | for: new -->\n\nMake dictation sound like you: casual in chat, careful in email.\n\nTry saying: "be more casual in Slack"\n\n1. Open **Style**.\n2. Choose how formal she writes in each kind of app, and how much she tidies.\n\n## Snippets\n\n<!-- id: snippets | task: insert text I type often | status: live | area: talk | place: snippets | on: desktop, voice | for: new -->\n\nSay a short cue and the text you saved lands where you are typing: an address, a link, a sign-off.\n\nTry saying: "make a snippet called my address" · "my address"\n\n1. Open **Snippets** and choose **New snippet**, or ask her to make one.\n2. While dictating, say the cue and the whole text is typed.\n\nGood to know: A snippet always types the same text. For text that changes, select it and use a transform.\n\n## Transforms\n\n<!-- id: transforms | task: rewrite selected text | status: live | area: talk | place: transforms | on: desktop, voice | for: new -->\n\nRewrite the text you have selected: polish it, shorten it or translate it.\n\nTry saying: "make this shorter" · "translate this to Urdu"\n\n1. Select text in any app.\n2. Press the transform shortcut, or ask her out loud.\n3. Say "undo that" to put the original back.\n\n## Scratchpad\n\n<!-- id: scratchpad | task: speak a quick note | status: live | area: talk | place: scratchpad | on: desktop, tessel, voice | for: new -->\n\nSpeak a quick note and find it again later.\n\nTry saying: "note that the boiler is due in March" · "find my note about the boiler"\n\n1. Ask her to note something from any device, or type it on the **Scratchpad** page.\n2. Search the page, or ask her what you noted.\n\n## Insights\n\n<!-- id: insights | task: see how I use voice | status: live | area: talk | place: insights | on: desktop | for: maker -->\n\nSee how much you dictate, how fast, and what she fixed, compared only with your own past.\n\nTry saying: "how much did I dictate this week?"\n\n1. Open **Insights**.\n\n## History\n\n<!-- id: history | task: find something I said | status: live | area: talk | place: history | on: desktop, web, voice | for: new | guide: tessaya-history.md -->\n\nFind something you said or asked, and copy or paste it again.\n\nTry saying: "what did I ask you yesterday?"\n\n1. Open **History** and search.\n2. Fix a word in a past dictation and she learns it.\n\n## Wake words\n\n<!-- id: wake | task: call her hands-free | status: live | area: talk | place: voice | on: desktop, tessel, voice | for: new | guide: tessaya-voice.md#start -->\n\nCall her by name, hands-free, on your computer or a Tessel.\n\nTry saying: "Hey Tessaya" · "change your wake word"\n\n1. Settings → Voice and wake words.\n2. Pick a wake word and the voice she answers in.\n\n## Just listen\n\n<!-- id: listen | task: think out loud without interruptions | status: live | area: talk | place: voice | on: desktop, tessel, voice | for: maker -->\n\nThink out loud without being interrupted: she only listens until you hand over.\n\nTry saying: "just listen, let me think out loud" · "over to you"\n\n1. Ask her to just listen.\n2. Say "over to you", or go quiet, and she answers the whole thought.\n\n## Personas and voices\n\n<!-- id: personas | task: choose who answers and how she sounds | status: live | area: talk | place: personas | on: desktop, web, phone, tessel, voice | for: new | guide: tessaya-voice.md#personas -->\n\nChoose who answers and how they sound. Each persona has its own voice and its own way of working.\n\nTry saying: "switch to Alfred" · "Freya, take this over"\n\n1. Open **Personas** to see each one with its voice.\n2. Call one by name, or ask one to take over what another started.\n\n## Groups\n\n<!-- id: groups | task: talk to several personas at once | status: live | area: talk | place: groups | on: desktop, web, voice | for: maker -->\n\nTalk to several personas at once; each answers in turn, in their own voice.\n\nTry saying: "start a group with Alfred and Freya"\n\n1. Open **Groups** and make one, or ask her to.\n\n## Sounds and cues\n\n<!-- id: cues | task: change her sounds | status: live | area: talk | place: voice | on: desktop, tessel, voice | for: maker | guide: voice-input.md -->\n\nChange her little sounds: how loud they are, or off, and the tones a Tessel\'s buttons make.\n\nTry saying: "make your sounds quieter" · "change the button sounds"\n\n1. Settings → Voice and wake words → Sounds.\n\n## The pill\n\n<!-- id: pill | task: see when she is listening | status: live | area: talk | place: appearance | on: desktop, phone | for: new | guide: tessaya-dictation.md#good-to-know -->\n\nThe small bar that shows when she is listening, what she heard and which window your words are for.\n\nTry saying: "make the pill quieter"\n\n1. Settings → Appearance → Pill design: Tessaya, Quiet or Lively, and the waveform you like.\n\n## Every setting by voice\n\n<!-- id: settings-voice | task: change a setting without clicking | status: live | area: talk | place: general | on: desktop, web, phone, tessel, voice | for: new -->\n\nChange any of her settings by asking. Some changes wait for your yes on your phone first.\n\nTry saying: "turn the volume up" · "turn wake words off" · "change it back"\n\n1. Ask for the change in your own words.\n2. She says what changed, and "change it back" undoes it.\n\n## Memory\n\n<!-- id: memory | task: have her remember things | status: live | area: know | place: memory | on: desktop, web, phone, tessel, voice | for: new | guide: tessaya-memory.md -->\n\nShe remembers what matters to you, and you can see, correct or forget any of it.\n\nTry saying: "remember that I like short answers" · "what do you know about me?" · "forget that"\n\n1. Tell her to remember something.\n2. Open **Memory** to search, correct or forget it.\n\n## What she has learned\n\n<!-- id: learned | task: see and correct her lessons | status: live | area: know | place: memory | on: desktop, web, voice | for: maker | guide: tessaya-memory.md#what-she-has-learned -->\n\nSee the lessons she took from your work, and correct the ones that are wrong.\n\nTry saying: "what have you learned this week?"\n\n1. Memory → What she has learned.\n\n## People, projects and Coming up\n\n<!-- id: upcoming | task: see what is coming up | status: live | area: know | place: upcoming | on: desktop, web, phone, tessel, voice | for: new -->\n\nOne list of everything that will happen later: reminders, jobs that run on their own, and what is due.\n\nTry saying: "what\'s coming up?" · "cancel that" · "undo"\n\n1. Open **Coming up**.\n2. Cancel or move anything on it; Undo brings back what you just cancelled.\n\n## Spelled names\n\n<!-- id: spelled | task: teach her how to spell a name | status: live | area: know | place: memory | on: desktop, tessel, voice | for: new -->\n\nTeach her how to spell a name by spelling it out loud.\n\nTry saying: "call me Zayd, Z-A-Y-D"\n\n1. Say the name, then spell it letter by letter.\n\n## Vault\n\n<!-- id: vault | task: keep passwords from every assistant | status: live | area: know | place: vault | on: desktop, web, phone | for: new | guide: tessaya-vault.md -->\n\nPasswords and keys she can use without seeing them, encrypted on this computer, with every use logged.\n\nTry saying: "put my GitHub token in the vault"\n\n1. Open **Vault** and add a key or a private note.\n\n## Privacy and what she keeps\n\n<!-- id: privacy | task: choose what she keeps and for how long | status: live | area: know | place: privacy | on: desktop, web, voice | for: new -->\n\nChoose what she keeps (recordings, what she notices on screen) and for how long.\n\nTry saying: "delete today\'s recordings" · "what do you keep about me?"\n\n1. Settings → Memory and privacy.\n2. Open **Forgotten** to see what was let go.\n\n## Household\n\n<!-- id: household | task: add someone who lives with me | status: live | area: know | place: privacy | on: desktop, web, phone, tessel, voice | for: home | guide: tessaya-voice.md#household -->\n\nAdd the people you live with. Each person has their own memory and their own yes.\n\nTry saying: "invite Sara to the household"\n\n1. Memory → Household → Invite.\n2. Anyone can leave, and take their own data with them.\n\n## Voice ID\n\n<!-- id: voiceid | task: have her know who is speaking | status: live | area: know | place: privacy | on: desktop, web, phone, tessel, voice | for: home | guide: tessaya-voice.md#voice-id -->\n\nShe knows who is speaking, so the right person\'s things come up.\n\nTry saying: "learn my voice" · "who am I?"\n\n1. Ask her to learn your voice and read the short passage she shows.\n\n## Face check\n\n<!-- id: faceid | task: confirm it\'s me with the camera | status: beta | area: know | place: privacy | on: desktop | for: maker | guide: tessaya-voice.md#face-check-windows -->\n\nConfirm it is you with the camera before something private, on Windows.\n\nTry saying: "check it\'s me"\n\n1. Memory → Household → Face check.\n\n## Now and Home\n\n<!-- id: now | task: see what she is doing now | status: live | area: today | place: now | on: desktop, web, phone | for: new -->\n\nSee what she is doing right now, and what needs you.\n\nTry saying: "what are you working on?" · "what needs me?"\n\n1. Open **Now** for what is running, or **Home** for your day.\n\n## Approvals\n\n<!-- id: approvals | task: approve or deny what she wants to do | status: live | area: today | place: approvals | on: desktop, web, phone, voice | for: new | guide: tessaya-jobs.md -->\n\nNothing runs without your yes. Everything waiting for you is here, with what it would do.\n\nTry saying: "what\'s waiting for me?" · "yes, go ahead"\n\n1. Open **Approvals**, read what it would do, then approve or say no.\n\n## Jobs\n\n<!-- id: jobs | task: hand her a job and come back later | status: live | area: today | place: jobs | on: desktop, web, phone, voice | for: new | guide: tessaya-jobs.md#start -->\n\nHand her a longer piece of work and come back later. She plans it first and asks before it starts.\n\nTry saying: "start a job to sort my downloads folder" · "every morning at 8, check the build and tell me what broke"\n\n1. Ask for the work in your own words.\n2. Approve the plan; the job shows on **Jobs** until it is done.\n\n## Who leads a job\n\n<!-- id: leads | task: see who is doing a job | status: live | area: today | place: jobs | on: desktop, web, voice | for: maker | guide: tessaya-jobs.md#who-leads-a-job -->\n\nSee which persona is on a job, and hand it to another.\n\nTry saying: "who\'s on this job?" · "give this to Onyx"\n\n1. Jobs → open a job to see who leads it.\n\n## Playbooks\n\n<!-- id: playbooks | task: have jobs get better each time | status: beta | area: today | place: jobs | on: desktop, web, voice | for: maker -->\n\nTell her what went wrong and the next job of that kind is done your way.\n\nTry saying: "that report was wrong, do it this way next time"\n\n1. Correct a finished job in your own words.\n\n## Alarms and wake-ups\n\n<!-- id: alarms | task: set an alarm or a wake-up | status: live | area: today | place: upcoming | on: tessel, voice | for: new -->\n\nAn alarm at a set time, rung on the Tessel nearest you.\n\nTry saying: "wake me up at 8:45" · "snooze" · "stop"\n\n1. Ask for the time. It shows in **Coming up**.\n\n## Cloud\n\n<!-- id: cloud | task: run work on another machine | status: live | area: today | place: cloud | on: desktop, web | for: builder | guide: cloud.md -->\n\nHand big jobs to a cloud computer and keep working here.\n\nTry saying: "run this in the cloud"\n\n1. Open **Cloud** to connect a machine and see what runs there.\n\n## Activity and why\n\n<!-- id: activity | task: see what she did and why | status: live | area: today | place: trust | on: desktop, web, tessel, voice | for: maker | guide: activity-log.md -->\n\nAsk what she did and why: every action she takes is logged with what caused it.\n\nTry saying: "what did you do in the last hour?" · "why did that happen?"\n\n1. Ask her, or open **Trust** to see the log.\n\n## Report a problem\n\n<!-- id: report | task: report a problem | status: live | area: today | place: health | on: desktop, web, phone, tessel, voice | for: new -->\n\nTell her something went wrong and she files one report with what she knows.\n\nTry saying: "report this" · "what reports have I made?"\n\n1. Say "report this" right after the problem.\n\n## Health\n\n<!-- id: health | task: find out why she is slow | status: live | area: today | place: health | on: desktop, web, voice | for: maker -->\n\nWhy she is slow or did not wake: her health and what to do about it.\n\nTry saying: "why are you slow?" · "why didn\'t you wake?"\n\n1. Open **Health**, or ask her.\n\n## Screen companion\n\n<!-- id: screen | task: get help with what\'s on my screen | status: live | area: agents | place: assistant | on: desktop, voice | for: new | guide: tessaya-screen.md -->\n\nGet help with what is on your screen: she can answer, show you each step, or do it while you watch.\n\nTry saying: "what\'s this error?" · "teach me how to export a PDF" · "do it for me"\n\n1. Ask about what you see. She asks before she looks unless you allowed it.\n2. Settings → Working for you sets what she may do.\n\n## Sessions\n\n<!-- id: sessions | task: watch and steer agent sessions | status: live | area: agents | place: sessions | on: desktop, web, phone, voice | for: builder | guide: tessaya-agents.md -->\n\nWatch and steer your coding agents\' sessions on every machine, and hear their answers where you are.\n\nTry saying: "what is the build session doing?" · "tell the build session to run the tests"\n\n1. Open **Sessions**, or ask her about a session by name.\n\n## Skills\n\n<!-- id: skills | task: see what she can do and add skills | status: live | area: agents | place: tools | on: desktop, web | for: maker -->\n\nSee what she can do, and add skills, plugins and servers.\n\nTry saying: "what skills do you have?" · "learn from that"\n\n1. Open **Skills**.\n\n## Trust\n\n<!-- id: trust | task: choose what runs without asking | status: live | area: agents | place: trust | on: desktop, web, voice | for: maker -->\n\nChoose what she may do without asking, and take any of it back.\n\nTry saying: "always ask before sending email" · "stop letting you look at my screen"\n\n1. Open **Trust**. Every standing yes is listed with a way to remove it.\n\n## Brain and usage\n\n<!-- id: usage | task: keep an eye on spend | status: live | area: agents | place: usage | on: desktop, web, voice | for: maker | guide: usage.md -->\n\nWhich model answers you, what it costs, and the spend guard that stops before a limit.\n\nTry saying: "how much have I spent today?" · "use Opus for this conversation"\n\n1. Open **Usage**, or Settings → Brain.\n\n## Accounts\n\n<!-- id: accounts | task: switch accounts or machines | status: live | area: agents | place: accounts | on: desktop, web, phone, voice | for: builder -->\n\nSwitch between your accounts, on every machine at once.\n\nTry saying: "switch to my other Claude account on every machine"\n\n1. Settings → Accounts.\n\n## Prompt Lab\n\n<!-- id: prompt-lab | task: edit and compare persona prompts | status: live | area: agents | place: lab:prompts | on: desktop, web, voice | for: maker -->\n\nEdit each persona\'s prompt and compare variants side by side. Making one live waits for your yes.\n\nTry saying: "open the prompt lab" · "try my variant B on Sonnet"\n\n1. Open **Lab** → Prompts.\n\n## Body playground\n\n<!-- id: playground | task: try her body moves | status: beta | area: agents | place: lab:body | on: desktop, web | for: builder | guide: tessaya-playground.md -->\n\nTry her body\'s moves and scenes, and let an agent drive them.\n\nTry saying: "wave at me"\n\n1. Open **Lab** → Body.\n\n## Outside agents\n\n<!-- id: outside | task: let other agents use Tessaya | status: live | area: agents | place: tools | on: desktop, web | for: builder | guide: tessaya-agents.md -->\n\nLet your other agents read what Tessaya knows and message her, through the same rules.\n\nTry saying: "let my terminal agent message you"\n\n1. See the guide for how an agent connects.\n\n## Connectors\n\n<!-- id: connectors | task: connect my calendar or mail | status: live | area: know | place: apis | on: desktop, web, voice | for: new | guide: tessaya-connectors.md -->\n\nConnect your calendar, mail and chat so she can answer about them.\n\nTry saying: "what\'s on my calendar tomorrow?"\n\n1. Settings → APIs and keys → Connectors.\n\n## APIs and keys\n\n<!-- id: apis | task: add an API key | status: live | area: agents | place: apis | on: desktop | for: maker -->\n\nAdd an API key for a provider she can use.\n\nTry saying: "add my OpenAI key"\n\n1. Settings → APIs and keys. Keys are encrypted on this computer.\n\n## One conversation everywhere\n\n<!-- id: conversation | task: carry on from another device | status: live | area: devices | place: home | on: desktop, web, phone, tessel, voice | for: new -->\n\nCarry on talking to her from another device; she remembers where you left off.\n\nTry saying: "carry on from the laptop"\n\n1. Just start talking on the other device.\n\n## Set up a Tessel\n\n<!-- id: tessel-setup | task: set up my Tessel | status: live | area: devices | place: hardware | on: desktop, phone, tessel | for: new | guide: home.md#set-up-a-tessel -->\n\nA Tessel (a Tumble, Tuft or Seed) is her body in the room, with her own voice and memory.\n\nTry saying: "add a Tessel"\n\n1. Plug it in.\n2. Open **Tessels** and add it with the digits shown on its eyes.\n\n## Tessel eyes and moods\n\n<!-- id: tessel-eyes | task: change how the Tessel looks | status: live | area: devices | place: hardware | on: tessel, voice | for: home -->\n\nHer eyes show how she feels and what she is doing.\n\nTry saying: "look at me" · "be sleepy"\n\n1. Ask her to; nothing to set up.\n\n## Tessel buttons\n\n<!-- id: tessel-buttons | task: choose what each button does | status: live | area: devices | place: hardware | on: desktop, tessel, voice | for: home -->\n\nChoose what each press, double press and long press does.\n\nTry saying: "make a double press of S1 start music"\n\n1. Tessels → your Tessel → Buttons, or ask her.\n\n## Tessel lights\n\n<!-- id: tessel-lights | task: dim the Tessel\'s light | status: live | area: devices | place: hardware | on: tessel, voice | for: home -->\n\nDim or brighten the Tessel\'s light.\n\nTry saying: "dim your light"\n\n## Tessel mic mute\n\n<!-- id: tessel-mute | task: make sure the Tessel isn\'t listening | status: live | area: devices | place: hardware | on: tessel, voice | for: home -->\n\nMake sure the Tessel is not listening.\n\nTry saying: "stop listening"\n\n1. Use the mute switch, or ask her. Her eyes show when the mic is off.\n\n## Headphones and speakers\n\n<!-- id: tessel-audio | task: use Bluetooth headphones | status: live | area: devices | place: hardware | on: desktop, tessel, voice | for: home -->\n\nPlay her voice through Bluetooth headphones or a speaker, and set how loud.\n\nTry saying: "play through my headphones" · "turn the volume up"\n\n1. Tessels → your Tessel → Audio.\n\n## Battery\n\n<!-- id: tessel-battery | task: check the battery | status: live | area: devices | place: hardware | on: tessel, voice | for: home -->\n\nCheck the battery. On battery she stays quiet, and tells you once when it is low.\n\nTry saying: "how\'s your battery?"\n\n## Tessel room\n\n<!-- id: tessel-room | task: tell her which room a device is in | status: live | area: devices | place: hardware | on: desktop, phone, tessel, voice | for: home -->\n\nTell her which room each device is in, so "the lights in here" means that room.\n\nTry saying: "you\'re in the kitchen"\n\n1. Tessels → your Tessel → Room, or tell her.\n\n## Tessel updates and repair\n\n<!-- id: tessel-update | task: update or repair a Tessel | status: live | area: devices | place: hardware | on: desktop, tessel | for: maker -->\n\nUpdate a Tessel, or repair one that will not start.\n\nTry saying: "update the Tessel"\n\n1. Tessels → your Tessel → Update.\n\n## Ask your computer from the Tessel\n\n<!-- id: laptop-ask | task: ask my laptop something from the Tessel | status: live | area: devices | place: hardware | on: tessel, voice | for: maker -->\n\nFrom across the room, ask the Tessaya on your computer about its screen or its work.\n\nTry saying: "ask the laptop what\'s on my screen"\n\n## Home Assistant\n\n<!-- id: homeassistant | task: control my home | status: live | area: devices | place: homeassistant | on: desktop, web, phone, tessel, voice | for: home | guide: home.md -->\n\nControl your lights and rooms by voice, and make automations in plain words.\n\nTry saying: "turn the kitchen lights off" · "make an automation for sunset"\n\n1. Open **Home Assistant** and connect it.\n\n## Intercom\n\n<!-- id: intercom | task: message people at home | status: live | area: devices | place: intercom | on: desktop, web, phone, tessel, voice | for: home | guide: tessaya-voice.md#messages-and-announcements -->\n\nSend a message to someone at home, spoken on their device.\n\nTry saying: "tell Sara dinner is ready"\n\n1. Open **Intercom** and turn messages on; they are off until you do.\n\n## Tessaya on your phone\n\n<!-- id: phone | task: use her on my phone | status: live | area: devices | place: phone | on: phone | for: new | guide: tessaya-phone.md -->\n\nTalk with her on the full screen, steer your work and see your personas and devices, away from the desk.\n\nTry saying: "pair my phone"\n\n1. Install the app.\n2. Open **Phone** in Tessaya\'s window and scan the code.\n\n## Away from home\n\n<!-- id: away | task: use her when I\'m out | status: live | area: devices | place: phone | on: phone, tessel, voice | for: home -->\n\nUse her when you are out: your phone reaches her on any of your machines.\n\nTry saying: "I\'m away from home"\n\n1. Pair your phone once; it finds her wherever she runs.\n';
export const DOCS_LESSONS_MD =
  '# Lessons\n\nShort lessons in Help, each a few steps that end in something working. A step ticks once you have\nused the page it teaches, on any of your devices. Each step names its feature in\n[Everything Tessaya does](tessaya-features.md).\n\n## Your first ten minutes\n\n<!-- id: first | for: new | minutes: 10 -->\n\nTalk to her, dictate one line, hand her one job. Three wins, then you know the shape of everything.\n\n1. **Say hello.** Say her name and ask anything; the pill wakes and she answers. Say "Hey Tessaya, what can you do?" <!-- wake -->\n2. **Dictate one line.** Click in any text box, hold Alt+Win, say a sentence, let go. Say "Lunch at one, new line, bring the charger" <!-- dictation -->\n3. **Hand her one job.** Ask for something that takes a few minutes; she plans it first. Say "Start a job to sort my downloads folder" <!-- jobs -->\n4. **Say yes.** Nothing runs without your yes. Read what it would do, then approve it. Say "Yes, go ahead" <!-- approvals -->\n\n## Set up your Tessel\n\n<!-- id: tessel | for: home | minutes: 8 -->\n\nPair it, wake it, make the buttons yours.\n\n1. **Pair it.** Plug it in and add it with the digits on its eyes. Say "Add a Tessel" <!-- tessel-setup -->\n2. **Wake it by name.** Stand anywhere in the room and call her. Say "Hey Tessaya, how\'s your battery?" <!-- wake -->\n3. **Pick your buttons.** Choose what a double or long press does. Say "Make a double press of S1 start music" <!-- tessel-buttons -->\n\n## Make dictation sound like you\n\n<!-- id: yours | for: maker | minutes: 6 -->\n\nStyle per app, a snippet, and rewriting what you have selected.\n\n1. **Set your style.** Casual in chat, careful in email. Say "Be more casual in Slack" <!-- style -->\n2. **Make a snippet.** One cue for text you type every day. Say "Make a snippet called my address" <!-- snippets -->\n3. **Rewrite a selection.** Select text anywhere and ask. Say "Make this shorter" <!-- transforms -->\n\n## Living together\n\n<!-- id: home | for: home | minutes: 7 -->\n\nAdd the people you live with, so she knows who is speaking and keeps each person\'s things apart.\n\n1. **Invite someone.** Each person gets their own memory and their own yes. Say "Invite Sara to the household" <!-- household -->\n2. **Teach her your voices.** A short guided read for each person. Say "Learn my voice" <!-- voiceid -->\n3. **Send a message home.** Messages are off until you turn them on. Say "Tell Sara dinner is ready" <!-- intercom -->\n\n## Let her work for you\n\n<!-- id: work | for: builder | minutes: 9 -->\n\nFrom "what\'s this error?" to jobs that run while you are away, and what she may do alone.\n\n1. **Ask about your screen.** Press the screen shortcut and ask. Say "What\'s this error?" <!-- screen -->\n2. **Steer a session.** Talk to an agent session without switching windows. Say "Tell the build session to run the tests" <!-- sessions -->\n3. **Choose what runs alone.** Trust decides what still asks you first. Say "Always ask before sending email" <!-- trust -->\n';
